#X text -177 546 This function Maps pitch/roll angle to the interval between drum samples. The interval decreases rapidly at small angles \, then gradually levels off as it approaches 1000 ms., f 29;
#X text 773 359 Raw pitch/roll values are divided by 1000 to fit within a reasonable coordinate range that suits the size of the drum corpus. The acceleration magnitude is also calculated and used as a multiplier to traverse the corpus faster \, if desired., f 41;
#X text 116 619 In this patch \, Yaw is split into sections. This ensures that only one drum voice is evolving at a time. For example \, if Yaw is at 180 degrees \, only the snare voice is being controlled by the user.;
